var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Guide","page":"Guide","text":"","title":"Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Requirements","page":"Guide","text":"Julia 1.10 or later.\nNo other packages. The Genie and HTTP.jl parts switch on by themselves when you load Genie 5 or 6, or HTTP.jl 1 or 2 (Julia calls these \"package extensions\").\nA Privatus Analytics site id (it starts with pa_). You find it under Site settings, Tracking.","title":"Requirements"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Install","page":"Guide","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"PrivatusAnalytics\")\n\nor type ] add PrivatusAnalytics in the Julia REPL. For the full setup guide and every tracker option, see the Privatus Analytics docs.\n\nSet your site id with an environment variable:\n\nPRIVATUS_SITE_ID=pa_YOURSITEID\n\nor in your code, once at startup:\n\nusing PrivatusAnalytics\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\")","title":"Install"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Add-the-tag","page":"Guide","text":"PrivatusAnalytics.tag() returns the tag. Put it in the <head> of your pages:\n\npage = \"\"\"\n<head>\n  <title>My app</title>\n  $(PrivatusAnalytics.tag())\n</head>\n\"\"\"\n\nIn production it prints:\n\n<script defer src=\"https://privatusstats.com/js/pa.js\" data-site=\"pa_YOURSITEID\"></script>\n\nThe tag prints nothing when there is no site id, and nothing outside production (see below). With queue_stub = true it then prints only the queue stub (see Track from your own JavaScript). The result is a SafeHTML string: it works anywhere a string works, and tools like Pluto, Jupyter and Documenter show it as HTML.","title":"Add the tag"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Genie","page":"Guide","text":"Load the package next to Genie, for example in config/initializers/privatus.jl:\n\nusing PrivatusAnalytics\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\")\n\nThen put the helper in the <head> of your layout, for example app/layouts/app.jl.html:\n\n<head>\n  <title>My app</title>\n  <% privatus_analytics_tag() %>\n</head>\n\nUse <% ... %> here, not $(...). Genie reads the layout as HTML, and text written with $(...) inside <head> gets moved into the <body>.\n\nprivatus_analytics_tag returns Genie's own HTML string type, and it passes the current Genie request to your props function (see Page props).","title":"Genie"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#HTTP.jl","page":"Guide","text":"Call tag in your handler. Pass the request if your props need it:\n\nusing HTTP, PrivatusAnalytics\n\nfunction home(req)\n    html = \"<html><head><title>Home</title>$(PrivatusAnalytics.tag(request = req))</head><body>Hi</body></html>\"\n    return HTTP.Response(200, [\"Content-Type\" => \"text/html; charset=utf-8\"], html)\nend","title":"HTTP.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Or-let-the-package-add-it","page":"Guide","text":"If you would rather not touch your layouts, let the package add the tag for you. In a Genie app, switch on auto_inject:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\", auto_inject = true)\n\nWith HTTP.jl, wrap your handler or router in the middleware:\n\nusing HTTP, PrivatusAnalytics\n\nrouter = HTTP.Router()\nHTTP.register!(router, \"GET\", \"/\", home)\nHTTP.serve(PrivatusAnalytics.middleware(router), \"0.0.0.0\", 8080)\n\nBoth add the tag just before </head> in uncompressed text/html responses with status 200, and set Content-Length to the new size. They skip Ajax requests (with the X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest header), pages without a <head>, and pages that already have the tag. Responses that have a Content-Encoding header (compressed responses) are left alone, so compress after the middleware, or use the helper instead. The middleware works with request handlers, not stream handlers.\n\nThe middleware reads the settings on each request. You can also give it its own settings and a Content Security Policy nonce (a string, or a function that gets the request):\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.middleware(router; nonce = req -> nonce_for(req))","title":"Or let the package add it"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Static-sites:-Franklin-and-Documenter","page":"Guide","text":"For a static site, the tag is written when you build the site, so set PRIVATUS_ENV=production in the build that you publish (for example in your GitHub Actions deploy job). Local builds then stay out of your reports.","title":"Static sites: Franklin and Documenter"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Franklin.jl","page":"Guide","text":"Add an HTML function to utils.jl:\n\nusing PrivatusAnalytics\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\", props = (section = \"blog\",))\n\nhfun_privatus() = String(PrivatusAnalytics.tag())\nhfun_privatus_click(params) = String(click_attr(params[1]))\n\nThen call it in the head of _layout/head.html:\n\n<head>\n  <title>{{fill title}}</title>\n  {{privatus}}\n</head>\n\nand name the parts you care about for click maps in your layout files, like <a href=\"/pricing/\" {{privatus_click nav.pricing}}>Pricing</a>.","title":"Franklin.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Documenter.jl","page":"Guide","text":"Documenter 1.13 and later can put raw HTML in the head with RawHTMLHeadContent. In docs/make.jl:\n\nusing Documenter, PrivatusAnalytics\n\nprivatus = String(PrivatusAnalytics.tag(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\"))\n\nmakedocs(\n    sitename = \"MyPackage.jl\",\n    format = Documenter.HTML(assets = isempty(privatus) ? [] : [RawHTMLHeadContent(privatus)]),\n)\n\nIf your Documenter version has no RawHTMLHeadContent, add the tracker as a script asset instead. This way has no page props:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\")\ntracker = asset(\"https://privatusstats.com/js/pa.js\"; class = :js,\n                attributes = Dict(:defer => \"\", Symbol(\"data-site\") => \"pa_YOURSITEID\"))\nassets = PrivatusAnalytics.render() ? [tracker] : []\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.render() is true when there is a site id and the tag is on.\n\nStatic pages from any other tool can go through PrivatusAnalytics.inject(html), which adds the tag before </head>.","title":"Documenter.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Configuration","page":"Guide","text":"Every setting is optional except the site id.\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(\n    site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\",                 # or ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SITE_ID\"]\n    script_host = \"https://privatusstats.com\", # or ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SCRIPT_HOST\"]\n    modules = [\"engage\", \"auto\", \"vitals\", \"clicks\", \"ask\"],\n    excluded_paths = [\"/admin/*\", \"/preview/*\"],\n    domains = [\"example.com\", \"www.example.com\"],\n    spa = \"auto\",          # auto, history, hash or off\n    manual = false,        # true turns off the automatic pageview\n    enabled = nothing,     # true or false forces the tag on or off\n    auto_inject = false,   # Genie only\n    extra_attributes = Dict(\"data-mask\" => \"/orders/*->/orders/:id\"),\n    props = req -> (plan = plan_for(req),),\n    queue_stub = false,\n    nonce = nothing,\n)\n\nSetting Default What it does\nsite_id ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SITE_ID\"] The data-site attribute. Nothing prints without it\nscript_host https://privatusstats.com Where /js/pa.js is served. Change it only if you host your own copy\nmodules tracker default (engage) The data-modules attribute. Setting it replaces the default, so keep engage for time on page and scroll depth. String[] loads none\nexcluded_paths none The data-exclude attribute. Path globs the tracker never counts\ndomains all hosts The data-domains attribute. Count only these hostnames\nspa auto The data-spa attribute (for single-page apps)\nmanual false The data-manual attribute\nenabled nothing true or false forces the tag on or off. nothing means on only when ENV[\"GENIE_ENV\"] == \"prod\" or ENV[\"PRIVATUS_ENV\"] == \"production\"\nauto_inject false Adds the tag to every HTML page of a Genie app. With HTTP.jl, use middleware\nextra_attributes none Any other data-* attribute\nprops none Page props sent with every pageview and event. A NamedTuple, a Dict, or a function that gets the request. See below\nqueue_stub false Prints a small script first, so privatus.track calls made before the tracker loads are kept and sent later\nnonce nothing A Content Security Policy (CSP) nonce for the script tags. A string, or a function that gets the request\n\nEach tracker attribute is explained in the script attributes reference, and the modules in Modules.\n\nYou can also change any setting for one call:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.tag(modules = [\"engage\", \"auto\"], excluded_paths = [\"/preview/*\"])","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Development-and-test","page":"Guide","text":"Requests are only counted in production by default, so your own clicking around never reaches your reports. Genie sets GENIE_ENV=prod in production. Elsewhere, set PRIVATUS_ENV=production. To see the tag while you build, set enabled = true. The tracker also ignores localhost unless you pass data-allow-local or data-debug (see Debug mode):\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(enabled = true, extra_attributes = Dict(\"data-debug\" => \"true\"))","title":"Development and test"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Leaving-people-out","page":"Guide","text":"Use data-exclude through excluded_paths for admin areas. To leave out signed-in staff, print the tag only for other people:\n\n<% is_staff() ? \"\" : privatus_analytics_tag() %>","title":"Leaving people out"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Product-analytics:-see-which-features-people-use","page":"Guide","text":"Privatus Analytics can show which buttons, forms and features people really use. You add a few attributes to your HTML. The tracker reads them in the browser and sends the events. Your server still sends nothing.","title":"Product analytics: see which features people use"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Name-events-well","page":"Guide","text":"Use a short \"Noun verb\" name, like Report exported or Invite sent. Put the details in props, not in the name. So write Report exported with format = \"csv\", not Report exported as CSV. Then all exports add up in one place, and you can split them by format.","title":"Name events well"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Events-on-buttons,-links-and-forms","page":"Guide","text":"event_attrs prints the attributes inside a tag you write yourself:\n\n\"<button $(event_attrs(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\", source = \"toolbar\"))>Export</button>\"\n\nIt prints:\n\n<button data-privatus-event=\"Report exported\" data-privatus-prop-format=\"csv\" data-privatus-prop-source=\"toolbar\">Export</button>\n\nProps can be keywords, a NamedTuple or a Dict. A NamedTuple and keywords keep their order. A Dict has no order, so its keys are sorted.\n\nevent_data returns the same attributes as a list of name => value pairs, with the values not escaped yet, for HTML builders that escape for you.\n\nIn Genie views, use privatus_event_data with Genie's HTML functions. Genie prints attribute values as they are, so this one escapes them for you:\n\n<% Html.button(\"Export\"; class = \"btn\", privatus_event_data(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\")...) %>\n\nOn a form, the event is sent when the form is submitted:\n\n\"<form action=\\\"/newsletter\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" $(event_attrs(\"Newsletter joined\"; list = \"weekly\"))>\"\n\nThe rules:\n\nThe name is trimmed and cut to 120 characters. An empty name prints nothing.\nProp keys are made lowercase. Anything that is not a letter, a digit or _ becomes _, so \"Report Type\" becomes report_type. Keys are cut to 64 characters.\nAt most 30 props. Values become text: true, false, numbers as written, lists joined with commas. nothing and missing values are left out. Values are cut to 500 characters.\nEverything is escaped for HTML.\nThe attributes print everywhere, even when the tag is off. They do nothing without the tracker, so your pages look the same in development and production.","title":"Events on buttons, links and forms"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Click-maps","page":"Guide","text":"A click map shows where people click on a page. Give the important parts a name so they stay easy to find, even when the page changes:\n\n\"<a href=\\\"/pricing\\\" $(click_attr(\"pricing.cta\"))>See plans</a>\"\n\n<% Html.a(\"See plans\"; href = \"/pricing\", privatus_click_data(\"pricing.cta\")...) %>\n\nA name may use letters, digits and _ . : -, up to 100 characters. Anything else prints nothing, and outside production the package logs a warning.","title":"Click maps"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Page-props:-plan,-role-and-other-groups","page":"Guide","text":"Page props are sent with every pageview and event on the page. Use them to split your reports by plan, role, app version, feature flag or account tier.\n\nSet them for every page with a function. It runs on each request and gets the request (an HTTP.Request in Genie and HTTP.jl):\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(props = req -> (plan = plan_for(req), role = role_for(req), app_version = \"2.4\"))\n\nA function with no arguments works too, and so does a plain NamedTuple or Dict. You can also set or change props for one page. They are merged over the configured ones, and nothing removes one:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.tag(props = (section = \"billing\", role = nothing))\n\nThe tag then prints a small script before the tracker, with your Content Security Policy nonce when you have one, and points the tracker at it:\n\n<script nonce=\"...\">window.privatusPageProps=function(){return {\"plan\":\"pro\",\"role\":\"admin\"}}</script>\n<script defer src=\"https://privatusstats.com/js/pa.js\" data-site=\"pa_YOURSITEID\" data-props=\"privatusPageProps\"></script>\n\nKeys follow the same rules as event props. Numbers and true or false stay as they are, and lists stay lists (up to 30 items). The props are escaped so they are safe inside a script. The middleware and Genie's auto_inject use the same setting.\n\nNever put names, emails, user ids or anything that points to one person in props. Privatus Analytics counts visitors without any id. Put groups (like the plan or the role), not people. The server also removes emails and long ids it finds.","title":"Page props: plan, role and other groups"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Track-from-your-own-JavaScript","page":"Guide","text":"For things that are not a click or a submit, call the tracker from your JavaScript, as the JavaScript API docs explain:\n\nprivatus.track(\"Feature used\", { feature: \"export\" })\n\nIf your code may run before the tracker has loaded, switch on the queue stub. It prints a tiny script before the tracker that keeps your calls in a list and sends them once the tracker is ready:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(queue_stub = true)\n\nor for one page: PrivatusAnalytics.tag(queue_stub = true). The stub prints even when the tag is off (in development, or with no site id). Then the tag prints only the stub, with no tracker, so your privatus.track(...) calls never fail. They wait in the list and are never sent.","title":"Track from your own JavaScript"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#See-the-results","page":"Guide","text":"Funnels: how many people go from one step to the next.\nClick maps: where people click.\nGoals: turn an event into a goal to count conversions.\nEvents: every custom event and its props.","title":"See the results"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Privacy","page":"Guide","text":"The script sets no cookies and stores nothing in the browser. The event, click and props helpers only print HTML attributes and a small script. Keep people out of your props and event props: no names, emails or user ids. See the privacy documentation for what is collected.\n\nIf you have a privacy policy, it should say which tools handle your visitors' data. You can paste this:\n\nThis website uses Privatus Analytics to count visits. It does not use cookies and does not follow you from one website to another. Your IP address is used for a moment to count visits and is never stored.\n\nChange it to fit your site. The privacy policy generator makes a longer version with your site's name in it.","title":"Privacy"},{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"module","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.PrivatusAnalytics","page":"Reference","text":"PrivatusAnalytics\n\nAdds the cookieless Privatus Analytics tracking script to Julia web apps and sites.\n\nThe package only prints HTML: the browser script tag and a few data attributes. It never sends events from the server, sets no cookies and reads nothing about your visitors.\n\nStart with configure! and tag. See the README for Genie, HTTP.jl, Franklin and Documenter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.PrivatusAnalytics"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.Configuration","page":"Reference","text":"Configuration(; kwargs...)\n\nSettings for the tracking script. Every setting is optional except the site id.\n\nsite_id: the site id (starts with pa_). Falls back to ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SITE_ID\"].\nscript_host: origin that serves /js/pa.js. Falls back to ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SCRIPT_HOST\"], then https://privatusstats.com.\nmodules: tracker modules to load, for example [\"engage\", \"auto\"]. nothing keeps the tracker default. String[] loads none.\nexcluded_paths: path globs the tracker never counts, for example [\"/admin/*\"].\ndomains: hostnames to count. nothing counts every host.\nspa: one of \"auto\", \"history\", \"hash\", \"off\". nothing keeps the tracker default.\nmanual: true turns off the automatic pageview.\nenabled: true or false forces the tag on or off. nothing turns it on only when ENV[\"GENIE_ENV\"] == \"prod\" or ENV[\"PRIVATUS_ENV\"] == \"production\".\nauto_inject: true adds the tag to every HTML page of a Genie app.\nextra_attributes: other data-* attributes, for example Dict(\"data-mask\" => \"/orders/*->/orders/:id\").\nprops: page props sent with every pageview and event, for example (plan = \"pro\",). A NamedTuple, Dict or list of pairs, or a function called on each request: req -> (plan = plan_for(req),). Never put names, emails, user ids or anything else that points to one person here.\nqueue_stub: true prints the tracker's queue stub first, so privatus.track works before pa.js loads.\nnonce: a Content Security Policy nonce for the script tags. A string, or a function called on each request.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.Configuration"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.SafeHTML","page":"Reference","text":"SafeHTML(html)\n\nA string of HTML that is already escaped and safe to print as is.\n\nIt works anywhere a String works (string interpolation, print, *, HTTP bodies), and it shows as real HTML in tools that understand the text/html MIME type, like Pluto, Jupyter and Documenter @example blocks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.SafeHTML"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.click_attr-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"click_attr(name) -> SafeHTML\n\nThe click map name attribute as escaped HTML: data-privatus-click=\"pricing.cta\". Prints nothing when the name is not valid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.click_attr"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.click_data-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"click_data(name) -> Vector{Pair{String,String}}\n\nThe click map name as \"data-privatus-click\" => name, or an empty list when the name is not valid. Outside production it logs a warning for a name that is not valid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.click_data"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.configuration-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"configuration() -> Configuration\n\nThe global settings used by tag and the integrations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.configuration"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.configure!-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"configure!(; kwargs...) -> Configuration\n\nChanges the global settings. Takes the same keywords as Configuration.\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\", modules = [\"engage\", \"auto\"])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.configure!"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.escape_html-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"escape_html(value) -> String\n\nEscapes & < > \" ' so a value is safe inside an HTML attribute or element.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.escape_html"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.event_attrs","page":"Reference","text":"event_attrs(name, props = nothing; more_props...) -> SafeHTML\n\nData attributes for a custom event, as escaped HTML to put inside a tag:\n\n\"<button $(event_attrs(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\"))>Export</button>\"\n\nOn a <form> the event is sent when the form is submitted. Prints nothing for an empty name. The attributes print even when the tag is off, so your pages look the same everywhere.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.event_attrs"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.event_data","page":"Reference","text":"event_data(name, props = nothing; more_props...) -> Vector{Pair{String,String}}\n\nThe custom event attributes as attribute name => value pairs, with values not yet escaped. Use it with HTML builders that escape values for you. Returns an empty list for an empty name.\n\nevent_data(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\")\n# [\"data-privatus-event\" => \"Report exported\", \"data-privatus-prop-format\" => \"csv\"]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.event_data"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.inject","page":"Reference","text":"inject(html, config = configuration(); request = nothing, overrides...) -> String\n\nPuts the tag just before </head>. Leaves the page alone when it already has the tag, has no </head>, or when the tag is off. Takes the same keywords as tag.\n\nHandy for static pages too, for example after a Franklin or Documenter build.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.inject"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.inject_response","page":"Reference","text":"inject_response(request, response; config = configuration(), nonce = nothing)\n\nAdds the tag to one HTTP.Response when injectable allows it. Used by middleware and by the Genie integration. Needs HTTP.jl.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.inject_response"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.injectable-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Reference","text":"injectable(status, content_type, content_encoding, requested_with) -> Bool\n\nWhether a response may get the tag: status 200, text/html, no Content-Encoding, and not an Ajax request (X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest). Missing headers are empty strings.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.injectable"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.isenabled","page":"Reference","text":"isenabled(config = configuration()) -> Bool\n\nWhether the tag should print. enabled wins when it is true or false. Otherwise the tag is on only when ENV[\"GENIE_ENV\"] == \"prod\" or ENV[\"PRIVATUS_ENV\"] == \"production\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.isenabled"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.isvalid_click-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"isvalid_click(name) -> Bool\n\nWhether a click map name is valid: letters, digits, _ . : - and at most 100 characters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.isvalid_click"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.middleware","page":"Reference","text":"middleware(handler; config = nothing, nonce = nothing)\n\nHTTP.jl middleware that adds the tag just before </head> in HTML responses. Needs HTTP.jl: run using HTTP first.\n\nusing HTTP, PrivatusAnalytics\nHTTP.serve(PrivatusAnalytics.middleware(router), \"0.0.0.0\", 8080)\n\nIt skips responses that are not status 200 text/html, compressed responses (with a Content-Encoding header), Ajax requests, pages without </head> and pages that already have the tag. It sets Content-Length to the new size. config defaults to the global settings at request time. nonce is a string, or a function that gets the request.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.middleware"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.normalize-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"normalize(props) -> Vector{Pair{String,Any}}\n\nCleans every key with normalize_key, drops nothing values and empty keys, and keeps the first 30 props.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.normalize"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.normalize_key-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"normalize_key(key) -> String\n\nLowercases a prop key, swaps anything outside a-z 0-9 _ for _ and cuts it to 64 characters. \"Report Type\" becomes \"report_type\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.normalize_key"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.page_props","page":"Reference","text":"page_props(config = configuration(), request = nothing)\n\nThe configured props for one request. Calls props when it is a function: with the request when it takes one argument, or with no arguments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.page_props"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.page_props_json-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"page_props_json(props) -> Union{String,Nothing}\n\nA JSON object string, or nothing when there are no props to send. <, >, &, U+2028 and U+2029 are written as \\u003c and so on, so the JSON is safe inside a <script>.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.page_props_json"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_analytics_tag","page":"Reference","text":"privatus_analytics_tag(; kwargs...)\n\nThe script tag for a Genie view, as a Genie ParsedHTMLString. Needs Genie: run using Genie first. It passes the current Genie request to a props or nonce function. Takes the same keywords as tag.\n\n<head>\n  <title>My app</title>\n  $(privatus_analytics_tag())\n</head>\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_analytics_tag"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_click_data","page":"Reference","text":"privatus_click_data(name) -> Vector{Pair{Symbol,String}}\n\nThe click map name for Genie's HTML functions, escaped. Empty when the name is not valid. Needs Genie.\n\n<% Html.a(\"See plans\"; href = \"/pricing\", privatus_click_data(\"pricing.cta\")...) %>\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_click_data"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_event_data","page":"Reference","text":"privatus_event_data(name, props = nothing; more_props...) -> Vector{Pair{Symbol,String}}\n\nThe custom event attributes for Genie's HTML functions (Html.button and friends), with every value already escaped, because Genie prints attribute values as they are. Needs Genie.\n\n<% Html.button(\"Export\"; class = \"btn\", privatus_event_data(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\")...) %>\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.privatus_event_data"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.render","page":"Reference","text":"render(config = configuration()) -> Bool\n\nWhether the tag prints: there is a site id and the tag is enabled.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.render"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.reset_configuration!-Tuple{}","page":"Reference","text":"reset_configuration!() -> Configuration\n\nPuts every setting back to its default. Handy in tests.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.reset_configuration!"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.script_attributes","page":"Reference","text":"script_attributes(config = configuration(), nonce = nothing) -> Vector{Pair{String,Any}}\n\nThe tracker tag's attributes, in order. true means an attribute without a value (defer).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.script_attributes"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.script_host","page":"Reference","text":"script_host(config = configuration()) -> String\n\nWhere /js/pa.js is served, without a trailing slash.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.script_host"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.site_id","page":"Reference","text":"site_id(config = configuration()) -> Union{String,Nothing}\n\nThe configured site id, else ENV[\"PRIVATUS_SITE_ID\"], else nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.site_id"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.tag","page":"Reference","text":"tag(config = configuration(); request = nothing, props = nothing, overrides...) -> SafeHTML\n\nThe Privatus Analytics script tag, as escaped HTML for the <head> of your page:\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.tag()\n# <script defer src=\"https://privatusstats.com/js/pa.js\" data-site=\"pa_YOURSITEID\"></script>\n\nWithout a site id, or when the tag is not enabled (see isenabled), prints only the queue stub when queue_stub is on, and otherwise nothing.\n\nAny setting of Configuration can be changed for this call, for example tag(modules = [\"engage\", \"auto\"], nonce = \"abc\").\nprops are merged over the configured props. A nothing value removes one.\nrequest is passed to a props or nonce function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.tag"},{"category":"method","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.to_html-Tuple{Any}","page":"Reference","text":"to_html(attrs) -> String\n\nTurns name => value pairs into HTML attributes, with every value escaped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.to_html"},{"category":"function","location":"reference/#PrivatusAnalytics.with_overrides","page":"Reference","text":"with_overrides(config; overrides...) -> Configuration\n\nA copy of config with some settings changed. The original is left alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.with_overrides"},{"category":"section","location":"#PrivatusAnalytics.jl","page":"Home","text":"Adds the cookieless Privatus Analytics tracking script to Julia web apps and sites: plain Julia, Genie, HTTP.jl, Franklin and Documenter.\n\nThe package only prints HTML: the browser script tag and a few data attributes. It never sends events from your server and sets no cookies.\n\nusing PrivatusAnalytics\nPrivatusAnalytics.configure!(site_id = \"pa_YOURSITEID\")\n\nPrivatusAnalytics.tag()\n# <script defer src=\"https://privatusstats.com/js/pa.js\" data-site=\"pa_YOURSITEID\"></script>\n\nevent_attrs(\"Report exported\"; format = \"csv\")\n# data-privatus-event=\"Report exported\" data-privatus-prop-format=\"csv\"\n\nclick_attr(\"pricing.cta\")\n# data-privatus-click=\"pricing.cta\"\n\nThe tag prints only in production: when ENV[\"GENIE_ENV\"] == \"prod\", ENV[\"PRIVATUS_ENV\"] == \"production\", or when you set enabled = true.\n\nThe Guide covers setup for each framework, configuration and product analytics. The Reference lists every exported function. The tracker itself is described in the Privatus Analytics docs and the script attributes reference.","title":"PrivatusAnalytics.jl"}]
}
